## 📌 Plain English Summary (Non-Legal)

> [!WARNING]
> This summary is for convenience only. The full license terms below are legally binding.

### ✅ What you _can_ do

- Use the software for **internal organisational purposes**
- View the source code **if you’ve been explicitly granted access**
- Make changes for **internal use only**
- Submit improvements via **pull requests** (if you have access)
- Share **small code snippets** for discussion or troubleshooting

### ❌ What you _cannot_ do

- Share the **full codebase**, or any substantial part of it
- Distribute **modified versions** of the software
- Host code outside **approved systems**
- Give access to unapproved users
- Use the software outside the organisation
- Offer the software to external parties

### ⚠️ Important boundaries

- Organisation membership ≠ access (approval required)
- Snippets are OK, but **not enough to reconstruct the system**
- The code is **confidential and must be protected**

### 🧾 Ownership

- Created by **Jason Moore**
- Jointly held with **Frederick Irwin Anglican School/AngliSchools**

### 🔒 In short

> [!NOTE]
> Internal use only. No redistribution. Access is controlled. Contributions go through PRs.

