## 🔐 Full License Terms

### 1. Ownership

This software, including all source code, binaries, documentation, and associated materials (the "Software"), is jointly held as follows:

- © **Jason Moore** (the "Author"), who retains original authorship and ongoing intellectual property rights
- **Frederick Irwin Anglican School/AngliSchools** (the "Organisation"), which retains ownership, control, and usage rights within its operational context

Ownership of the Software is **shared in tandem** between the Author and the Organisation, subject to the terms of this License.

All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

### 2. Grant of Use

The Organisation grants **authorized users** a limited, non-transferable, non-exclusive license to:

- Use the Software for internal purposes
- Access source code **only if explicitly approved**
- Modify the Software strictly for internal use

"Authorized users" are individuals explicitly granted access by the Author or Organisation.

### 3. Source Code Access and Sharing

Source code access is **restricted**.

You may:

- Access code only with explicit permission
- Use it within approved systems

You must NOT:

- Share the Software in whole or substantial part
- Host it outside approved systems
- Circumvent access controls

#### Permitted Limited Sharing

You may share **small snippets** if:

- They are non-substantial
- Used for discussion, review, or troubleshooting
- They cannot reconstruct the Software
- They do not expose sensitive logic

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Sharing functional modules or reconstructable portions is prohibited.

#### Anti-Reconstruction Clause

> Repeated or systematic sharing of snippets that collectively form a substantial portion is strictly prohibited.

#### Clarification

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Organisation membership does not grant access.

### 4. Restrictions

You may NOT:

- Distribute the Software (modified or not)
- Share modified versions
- Provide access outside approved systems
- Use it externally
- Offer it as a service
- Create externally distributed derivatives

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Modifications are strictly internal-use only.

### 5. Contributions

Authorized users may contribute via approved workflows (e.g., pull requests).

By contributing:

- Your contribution becomes part of the Software
- Rights are assigned to the Author and/or Organisation
- Contributions may be accepted, modified, or rejected

### 6. Distribution of Binaries

Only the Author and/or Organisation may:

- Build binaries
- Distribute artifacts

### 7. Access Control and Governance

The Organisation and/or Author control:

- Access permissions
- Approval and revocation
- Repository governance

Access grants **no additional rights** beyond this license.

### 8. Confidentiality

The Software is **confidential and proprietary**.

You must:

- Protect it from unauthorized disclosure
- Use it only as permitted

You must NOT:

- Disclose it in whole or substantial part
- Compromise its confidentiality

This obligation continues after termination.

### 9. Termination

This License terminates automatically on violation.

You must:

- Stop using the Software
- Delete all copies (including local clones)

### 10. Disclaimer

The Software is provided **"as is"**, without warranty of any kind.

### 11. Governing Law

This License is governed by the laws of **Western Australia, Australia**.

### 12. Author Retained Rights

**Subject to any separate written agreement between the Author and the Organisation**, the Author retains the right to:

- Store copies outside Organisation systems
- Maintain backups
- Retain copies after leaving
- Continue independent development

Upon leaving:

- The Organisation retains full rights to its version
- The Author may:
  - Continue development
  - Modify and evolve the code
  - Distribute and commercialise their version

#### Conditions

The Author must:

- Remove all Organisation-specific confidential information
- Not disclose internal logic or trade secrets
- Not imply affiliation
- Comply with applicable agreements

> The Organisation keeps its version; the Author is free to evolve theirs independently.

### 13. Third-Party Contributions

Contributions are allowed only via approved workflows.

#### Submission

Contributors confirm:

- They have the right to contribute
- Contributions do not infringe third-party rights

#### Assignment

All contributions:

- Become part of the Software
- Are assigned to the Author and/or Organisation
- May be used at their discretion

#### Contributor Rights

Contributors:

- Receive no ownership rights
- May not distribute their contributions independently

#### Restrictions

Contributors must NOT:

- Maintain external forks
- Distribute contributions
- Reconstruct the Software externally

#### Enforcement

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Contributions may be rejected or removed at any time for legal, security, or policy reasons.

#### Author Protection

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Contributions do not limit the Author’s independent rights under Clause 12.
